    <statement><p>Find the derivative of 
<m>\displaystyle f(t) = \frac{t^{3}+t^{4}-1}{t^{5}}</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(3t^{2}+4t^{3}\right)t^{5}-\left(t^{3}+t^{4}-1\right)\cdot 5t^{4}}{\left(t^{5}\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(t)</m>, we have 
<m>\frac{t^3 + t^4 - 1}{t^5} = t^{-2} + t^{-1} - t^{-5}</m>, so

<me>f'(t) = -2 t^{-3} - t^{-2} + 5 t^{-6}.</me>



</solution>
